.TH PERSISTENT-STOPWATCH 1 "August 2026" "persistent-stopwatch 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
persistent-stopwatch \- a stopwatch that keeps counting across restarts and reboots
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B persistent-stopwatch
[\fB\-\-start\fR] [\fB\-\-pause\fR] [\fB\-\-toggle\fR] [\fB\-\-lap\fR] [\fB\-\-reset\fR] [\fB\-\-status\fR] [\fB\-\-laps\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without options, opens the stopwatch window.
If the window is already open, it is raised instead of opening a second one.
.PP
The stopwatch does not count while it runs.
It stores the moment it was started and computes the elapsed time from that,
so closing the window, suspending or rebooting the machine does not stop it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-start
Start the stopwatch, or resume it if paused.
.TP
.B \-\-pause
Pause the stopwatch.
.TP
.B \-\-toggle
Pause the stopwatch if it is running, start it otherwise.
Handy as the command behind a single global shortcut.
.TP
.B \-\-lap
Record a lap. Ignored unless the stopwatch is running.
.TP
.B \-\-reset
Reset the stopwatch to zero and clear all laps.
.TP
.B \-\-status
Print the state, the elapsed time and when the stopwatch was started,
for example
.BR "Running 00:12:03.4 (started 2026-08-06T09:12:44)" ,
then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-laps
Print the recorded laps, oldest first, one per line: the lap number, the
lap's own time and the total elapsed time, separated by tabs.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the state, the elapsed time in milliseconds, the start time and the
laps as a single JSON object, for scripts and status bars. Replaces the
output of
.B \-\-status
and
.BR \-\-laps .
.PP
Action options can be combined. They are applied in the order reset, start,
toggle, lap, pause, so
.B "\-\-reset \-\-start"
always restarts from zero.
Actions are applied to the saved state, and the program exits without
opening a window. If the window is open, it notices the change and
follows along.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
In the window:
.TP
.B Space
Start or pause.
.TP
.B L
Record a lap.
.TP
.B R
Reset. A notification offers to undo it.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Z
Undo the last reset.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, including actions that do nothing in the current state
(for example
.B \-\-lap
while paused). Nonzero for an unknown option, or if the window fails to
load.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QT_QUICK_CONTROLS_STYLE
Overrides the Qt Quick Controls style. By default the KDE desktop style is
used when it is installed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/persistentstopwatchstaterc
The saved state. Written on every change.
.SH EXAMPLES
Time a long build:
.PP
.RS
.nf
persistent-stopwatch \-\-reset \-\-start
make
persistent-stopwatch \-\-pause \-\-status
.fi
.RE
.PP
Get the fastest lap from a run:
.PP
.RS
.nf
persistent-stopwatch \-\-laps | sort \-t "$(printf '\\t')" \-k2 | head \-1
.fi
.RE
.PP
Show the elapsed minutes in a status bar:
.PP
.RS
.nf
persistent-stopwatch \-\-json | jq '.elapsedMs / 60000 | floor'
.fi
.RE
